Windows does not ship the toolkit's default Open Sans and Noto Sans Mono
families. These unmodified fonts are embedded on Windows so interface/proof
text uses the requested families, including in existing pixel regressions.

Source: Fedora 44 open-sans-fonts 1.10-25, google-noto-sans-mono-fonts 20251201-2,
and google-noto-sans-mono-vf-fonts 20251201-2, from Neo's installed font packages.
Copyright and redistribution terms are in LICENSE.OpenSans (Apache 2.0) and
LICENSE.Noto (SIL Open Font License 1.1). The Noto copyright and license are
recorded in each font's name table; the included OFL text carries that notice.
Font file name tables retain their upstream notices.
Linux continues to use its installed fonts.

The regular face is the original variable NotoSansMono[wght].ttf, SHA256
3c874b97ce11dc54de004c81df02c8f0974033ed1b113377130cbdd71d478f11.
A cosmic-text 0.19 shaping probe on Neo selects that file for normal weight 400
and the static NotoSansMono-Bold.ttf for weight 700. Bundling the static regular
face instead changes unstyled glyph rasterization and fails the preserved
Neo pixel fixtures. No visual baseline was regenerated for this Windows port.
